    "body": "Fixes #42521\n\n## Problem\n`vim.system(cmd, { timeout = N })` kills the child almost immediately (1-2 ms) when Lua code blocked the event loop for longer than N ms before the call, returning code 124 / signal 15.\n\n## Root cause\n`run()` in `runtime/lua/vim/_core/system.lua` arms the timeout timer right after `uv.spawn` without refreshing libuv's cached loop time. libuv measures timer deadlines from the cached loop clock, so the timer is already overdue when started.\n\n## Fix\nCall `uv.update_time()` before arming the timeout timer in `vim.system`.\n\n## Tests\n- Reporter's repro (headless `nvim -l`): before fix, a 1200 ms block before a 500 ms timeout yields ~1 ms; after fix, ~500 ms as expected.\n- New functional test `timeout is measured from spawn, not from stale loop time #42521` in `test/functional/lua/system_spec.lua`: passes with the fix, fails without it (verified by rebuilding without the fix). Full file run: 17 passed, 1 pre-existing skip.\n- Verified on Linux x86_64 with a self-built Release binary; the reporter reproduced on macOS arm64, but I have no macOS machine to verify there (the fix is loop-time logic only, platform-independent).\n\n## AI assistance disclosure\nThis PR was developed with AI assistance.",
